- Story & Context: Legend has it that when the old coastal semaphore tower finally collapsed into the sea near Port Blossom, its final, rusted arm pointed directly towards the deepest point in the North Channel, a silent, defiant instruction for all the lost vessels and their forgotten crews, echoing the final broadcast of a storm-battered lighthouse. "We broadcast our silence, hoping someone hears."
